<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Infographic illustrating mechanisms of lytic and non-lytic neutrophil extracellular trap \(NET\) formation, highlighting pathways including receptors, NOX complex, ROS, chromatin decondensation, PAD4 involvement, vesicle-mediated secretion, membrane disruption, and eventual NET release, with lytic leading to cell death and non-lytic preserving cell integrity.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Infographic illustrating neutrophil origin in bone marrow, migration through endothelium, and tissue entry; four neutrophil subtypes with distinct characteristics; major functions including phagocytosis, degranulation, ADCC, and extracellular trap formation; and a central diagram linking infection and reactive oxygen species \(ROS\) production to both protective \(pathogen clearance\) and pathological \(tissue injury, sepsis\) outcomes.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
